WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.680
Welcome to our training on culturally respectful listings.

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:08.880
When you list products in the Amazon store, it's important to consider not just what you sell,

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:10.960
but also how you present it.

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:14.080
Customers seek out products that are meaningful to them.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:14.947
Think about it.

00:00:14.947 --> 00:00:19.280
When you see an advertisement for a product or a package on a store shelf,

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:23.520
you're more likely to buy the product if the advertisement or the package

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:25.467
shows something important to you.

00:00:25.467 --> 00:00:29.360
When you sell a product that represents a particular culture,

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:34.320
demonstrating that you understand and respect that cultural connection can make your product

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:38.000
more appealing to your customers, which can help drive sales.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:39.840
For example, imagine that you're

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:43.173
selling a dress in the style of Chinese formal wear.

00:00:43.173 --> 00:00:45.840
If you use models in your product images,

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:51.186
using models from that same culture shows customers that you have a knowledge of your product's

00:00:51.186 --> 00:00:51.520
origins

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:54.895
and appreciate the context in which it was created.

00:00:54.895 --> 00:00:57.520
This can build customer trust and loyalty,

00:00:57.520 --> 00:01:03.040
which are good for both your business and for customers who choose to shop in the Amazon store.

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:05.520
This isn't just true for clothing.

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:08.000
Toys, jewelry, and countless other products

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.867
can represent cultural traditions.

00:01:09.867 --> 00:01:13.600
Highlighting cultural connections not only makes your products

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:19.120
more appealing to customers from those cultures, but also can help customers who aren't familiar

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:21.981
with a particular culture see the product's value.

00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:23.769
This is another important point.

00:01:23.769 --> 00:01:25.200
Be aware of how

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:30.450
you sell products that are specific to one culture to customers from another culture.

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:31.200
Failing to

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:37.200
show that you understand or respect customers or their cultures can result in losing their trust

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:39.211
and driving them away.

00:01:39.211 --> 00:01:43.234
It may also violate Amazon's restricted products policies.

00:01:43.234 --> 00:01:44.240
For example,

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:49.280
showing photos of a culturally traditional garment on a non-native figure using negative

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:55.925
depictions such as blackface or unnaturally sexualizing or exaggerating parts of the garment could

00:01:55.925 --> 00:01:56.400
upset

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:58.475
customers and violate our policies.

00:01:58.475 --> 00:02:03.040
Finally, when you create a listing, think about not only what

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:06.155
you're selling, but also where you're selling it.

00:02:06.155 --> 00:02:08.880
If you're selling in an international store,

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:14.560
be aware that the expectations of your customers might be different from what you're used to.

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:18.507
Also, be aware that these expectations may change over time.

00:02:18.507 --> 00:02:20.480
In the US, for example,

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:26.480
some professional sports teams used names, images, and slogans that were disrespectful toward Native

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:26.885
Americans.

00:02:26.885 --> 00:02:31.741
Some of those sports teams have since rebranded to be more respectful.

00:02:31.741 --> 00:02:33.360
If you were reselling

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:39.200
products relating to those teams, you should show your respect for Native Americans, these teams,

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:44.400
and your customers by avoiding the names, images, or slogans that are no longer used.

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:51.360
As another example, a popular drink in Europe used images of an African man on its packaging

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:53.527
that drew on negative stereotypes.

00:02:53.527 --> 00:02:56.560
Customers were rightfully upset by these images.

00:02:57.280 --> 00:03:01.920
As a result, the company changed the image on its packaging to be more respectful.

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:05.732
Negative attention can damage a brand and draw press attention.

00:03:05.732 --> 00:03:07.840
It can then take a long time

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:11.790
to earn back a customer's loyalty once it's been lost.

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:14.160
Always remember that your customers are

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:19.440
people, and that delighting as many of your customers as possible is your highest priority.

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:24.400
Taking care to show respect for specific products and different cultures

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:29.520
may mean doing a little extra work, but imagine the benefit it can have for customers and your

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:30.051
business.

00:03:30.051 --> 00:03:34.298
This concludes our training on culturally respectful listings.

00:03:34.298 --> 00:03:35.360
Thank you,

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:37.760
and happy selling in the Amazon Store.
